# Model Sentinel launchd environment bootstrap.
#
# Live file location after ./setup_launchd.sh:
#   ~/.model_sentinel/launchd.env
#
# This file is sourced by the launchd runner script using bash.
# It may contain plain exports and/or shell commands that source another
# secrets file.
#
# Keep this file private:
#   chmod 600 ~/.model_sentinel/launchd.env
#
# File mode: configure MODEL_SENTINEL_CREDENTIAL_SOURCE=file in settings.env
# and refresh the private cache manually with model-sentinel credentials refresh.
# Scheduled scans read that static cache without opening the refresh mount.
# Keep unrelated exports such as PATH here. This file is executable Bash, not
# assignment-only credential input. Setup preserves existing bootstrap lines;
# remove obsolete secret bootstrap lines yourself when switching to file mode.
# The cache remains plaintext at rest (0700 parent, 0600 file).

# Environment mode option 1: source an existing secrets/bootstrap script.
# Example:
# source "$HOME/path/to/your/secrets.sh"

# Environment mode option 2: export the values directly here.
# Example:
# export OPENROUTER_AI_CREDS="..."
# export ABACUS_AI_CREDS="..."

